# Analytics (OpenPanel). Entirely optional.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the client id to switch analytics
# on. Leave it out and the site runs with no analytics and no third-party
# requests at all - which is the intended state for local development.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ values are inlined into the browser bundle at build time, so
# they have to be present when you build, not just when the server starts.
# On Vercel that means setting them in the project's environment variables and
# redeploying; a variable added after a build does not reach an existing one.

# Required to enable analytics. A public identifier, safe to expose - not the
# client secret, which is for server-side ingestion and must never be here.
NEXT_PUBLIC_OPENPANEL_CLIENT_ID=

# Self-hosted instance only. Set both, or neither: with only the API pointed at
# your own server the SDK script is still fetched from openpanel.dev, a domain
# tracker blockers recognise. Omit both to use OpenPanel's cloud.
NEXT_PUBLIC_OPENPANEL_API_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_OPENPANEL_SCRIPT_URL=
